Here's the .COM file I use to set things up:
===============================================================================
$ SET DEF SOL$DUA1:[AHABIG.NETHACK]
$ ASS SOL$DUA1:[AHABIG.NETHACK]TERMCAP. TERMCAP
$ DEF NETHACKOPTIONS "number_pad,name:''p1'"
===============================================================================

And here's the instructions I put in the NEWS. file :
===============================================================================
If playing from a PC keyboard, put NUMLOCK on.

When using SETUP.COM, put "'s around your name : eg.,

	@SETUP "Entropy-W"

makes you have a wizard named Entropy.  Omit the -W and a class is not
preassigned.

If you want other options set (such as female, packorder, etc), put them after
the name separated by a comma.  For example,

	@SETUP "Morgaine-W,female"

makes you a female wizard named Morgaine.
===============================================================================

